elf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T19:35:18-07:00","id":503734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demon Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/485979-advice-for-wod-and-exalted-table-decor?p=496736#post496736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow! I'm not familiar enough with the other games to offer good suggestions, but I really like what you're doing with the WW games.<br /> <br /> For Changeling: the Dreaming, how about some (fake) butterflies?<br /> Mismatched tea cups and plates<br /> eclectic odds &amp; ends (stroll through a junk shop and grab something that looks cool)<br /> something that glows, but shouldn't</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely like the idea of mismatched tea cups and plates. (Luckily, the plateware is done through my caterer and she said I can basically mix and match as much as I want, so I don't even have to worry about investing too much!) A butterfly motif could also be an interesting touch. Thank you! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/485979-advice-for-wod-and-exalted-table-decor?p=496791#post496791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Been thinking on this a bit, while I applaud the general goal and themes, I can't help but think every table a different theme, often completely different era/mythical setting, is going to be kinda clashing with itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see your point, but I also think it will probably work, precisely because EVERY table is different. It'll hopefully come out more as an eclectic look, rather than one that clashes too much. (Or so it does in my head. We'll see how real life works.) The location itself is really nice and I think kind of works with all of them, and I wasn't planning on doing too heavy decorations for the rest of the hallway, so hopefully it won't have too much conflict. We'll see, though. :x<br /> Thank you, it's something I'll try to consciously keep an eye on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2259-auroradragonkaya","name":"auroradragonkaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2259_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}